# smalltalk-playful-v1: Jokes and riddles, replies to laughter and playful teasing, and playful variants that join the light situations of the other collections (greetings, thanks, goodbyes, how-are-you, compliments).
# Generated by tools/smalltalk/build.mjs from tools/smalltalk/taxonomy.json and the accepted records of jobs/smalltalk-replies; do not edit by hand.

# The playful register: while the conversation's register is playful, whenever a situation applies its playful variant applies too, one priority higher, so it wins its part.
@stp_r_playful rule
  when cv_register playful
  when cv_applies ?s
  when st_playful_variant ?s ?v
  then cv_applies ?v

# Two variants tie as their bases do: the variant of the base that outranks the other outranks it too.
@stp_r_playful_ties rule
  when st_playful_variant ?a ?v
  when st_playful_variant ?b ?w
  when cv_situation_outranks ?a ?b
  then cv_situation_outranks ?v ?w

@stp_p_playful_joke fact
  holds cv_situation_priority playful_joke 78

@stp_k_playful_joke fact
  holds cv_courtesy_situation ask_joke playful_joke

